.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Dyson&#x27;s circular ensembles are built from Haar-random unitary matrices rather than Gaussian Hermitian ones: CUE (\beta=2) is simply the eigenvalue phases of a Haar-random U(n) matrix; COE (\beta=1) uses the symmetric unitary matrix U = V^T V for V Haar-random in U(n); CSE (\beta=4) uses the self-dual unitary U = V^R V built from a Haar-random V \in U(2n) (its 2n eigenvalues occur in doubly degenerate pairs, of which n distinct phases are kept). Because Haar measure is exactly rotation-invariant, the eigenvalue phases \theta \in [0, 2\pi) are, after rescaling by n/(2\pi), exactly unfolded to unit mean spacing at any finite n -- no asymptotic unfolding is needed, unlike the Gaussian/Wishart ensembles.">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/rmt/paper_replications/images/thumb/sphx_glr_circular_ensembles_demo_thumb.png
    :alt:

  :doc:`/api/gallery/rmt/paper_replications/circular_ensembles_demo`

.. raw:: html

      <div class="sphx-glr-thumbnail-title">Dyson's Circular Ensembles: COE, CUE, CSE</div>
    </div>


.. only:: not html

 * :doc:`/api/gallery/rmt/paper_replications/circular_ensembles_demo`

.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="The Ginibre ensembles GinOE (real), GinUE (complex), and GinSE (quaternion) drop the Hermitian/unitary symmetry constraint entirely: their n \times n matrices have i.i.d. Gaussian entries with no further structure, so eigenvalues are genuinely complex, spread over a two-dimensional region rather than confined to the real line or a circle. After rescaling by \sqrt{n} (Ginibre&#x27;s exact result, not just asymptotic), the eigenvalues fill the unit disk uniformly as n \to \infty -- the circular law. Because a uniform density on a disk is awkward to validate directly, this example instead checks the radial marginal: integrating out the angle, the magnitude r = |\lambda| has the simple closed-form density">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/rmt/paper_replications/images/thumb/sphx_glr_circular_law_demo_thumb.png
    :alt:

  :doc:`/api/gallery/rmt/paper_replications/circular_law_demo`

.. raw:: html

      <div class="sphx-glr-thumbnail-title">Ginibre's Circular Law</div>
    </div>


.. only:: not html

 * :doc:`/api/gallery/rmt/paper_replications/circular_law_demo`

.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="For a bi-unitarily-invariant non-Hermitian matrix M = U \, \mathrm{diag}(s_1, \dots, s_n)\, V, built from independent Haar-random unitary matrices U, V and singular values s_i, the single ring theorem states that as n \to \infty the eigenvalues fill the annulus r_{\text{in}} \leq |z| \leq r_{\text{out}}, with radii fixed by only the first two moments of the limiting singular-value distribution:">

